<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
        Two jobs, and the second one is not obvious.

        1. The window background is painted before Compose starts. This style
           used to be an empty DeviceDefault with no windowBackground, so the
           window came up in the device's default colour: a white flash on every
           cold start ahead of the dark splash. @color/app_background has a
           values-night twin, so it now matches whichever palette Compose is
           about to draw.

        2. The parent has to follow day and night, because a WebView reads
           `prefers-color-scheme` from the Activity theme's isLightTheme, not
           from the system. The parent was android:Theme.DeviceDefault, which is
           dark on every device — so the two bundled legal pages would have gone
           dark in light mode as well, which is why they were left light-only for
           everyone instead. Light here, plain DeviceDefault in values-night, and
           the media query in privacy_policy.html / terms_of_service.html tells
           the truth in both.

        Nothing else in the app reads this theme: every screen is Compose and
        takes its colours from LocalAstroColors.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.MyApplication" parent="android:Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/app_background</item>
    </style>

</resources>
